__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.env
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage

# The run's working directory, at the repository root only.
#
# Anchored, because an unanchored `data/` matches a directory of that name at
# every depth -- and this repository has one: `src/council/data/`, the price
# pipeline. That is how `data/fetch.py` sat untracked while `pyproject.toml`
# declared the dependency it needs, so a clone could install the study and not
# contain the step that downloads its input. Published artefacts live in
# `docs/results/` and are tracked deliberately; this pattern is only about the
# scratch directory a run writes into.
/data/
